{
  "_provenance": {
    "status": "SLUGS VERIFIED",
    "verifiedOn": "2026-08-20",
    "method": "Each slug fetched and checked for HTTP 200 plus a .forecast-table__table in the response. Four supplied directly by Brian.",
    "source": "snow-forecast.com",
    "notes": [
      "The per-resort key is a Snow-Forecast URL slug. Coordinates and elevations are no longer stored here \u2014 the scraper reads tier elevations off each page.",
      "Palisades is one entry backed by TWO slugs. Snow-Forecast still files the mountain under its former name Squaw-Valley and lists Alpine-Meadows separately; the real resort is the merged, lift-connected operation. Combined per the rule in `combine` below.",
      "Slugs follow no pattern. Taos and Revelstoke are bare; Whistler is Whistler-Blackcomb; Whiteface is Whiteface-Mountain. Never guess one \u2014 verify by fetching.",
      "`nws` is a point ON THE MOUNTAIN (mid-slope, not the base town) for api.weather.gov, US resorts only. NWS answers for the ~2.5km grid cell around it; scripts/fetch-weather.js rejects any point whose grid sits below the resort's base elevation, which is what a town forecast looks like. Added 2026-10-28.",
      "The four Cascades resorts (Mt. Baker, Crystal Mountain, Stevens Pass, Mt. Bachelor) were added 2026-10-29 from search results, not fetched: the sandbox cannot reach any of the three sources. Verified by scripts/check-new-resorts.sh on Brian's Mac before the first scrape that includes them. Crystal's OnTheSnow path is crystal-mountain-wa \u2014 plain crystal-mountain is the Michigan resort.",
      "Thirteen more added 2026-10-29 at Brian's pick \u2014 Tahoe (Sugar Bowl, Northstar, Mt. Rose, Sierra-at-Tahoe, Homewood), the Wasatch (Brighton, Solitude, Snowbasin, Powder Mountain) and Colorado (Vail, Breckenridge, Arapahoe Basin, Wolf Creek). Addresses from search results, checked by check-new-resorts.sh on his Mac before the first scrape. Snowbasin's Snow-Forecast slug is Snow-Basin; Wolf Creek's is Wolf-Creek-Ski-Area (Wolf-Creek-Utah is a different hill).",
      "`tz` (every resort) and `latlon` (the four Canadian resorts, which have no `nws` point) were added 2026-10-29 for the forecast archive: tz turns Snow-Forecast's local AM/PM/night periods into UTC, latlon is where the Open-Meteo ensembles are requested. The Canadian points are approximate mid-mountain coordinates from memory, not fetched; Open-Meteo is also given the Snow-Forecast mid elevation, so a few hundred metres of error in position matters little."
    ]
  },
  "tier": "mid",
  "combine": {
    "rule": "max",
    "why": "Where a resort has several slugs they are lift-connected faces of one mountain. If one side got 30cm and the other 10cm you ski the side that got it, so snow takes the max. Temp and wind also take the max because the warning thresholds are worst-case by design."
  },
